# Cursor Rules — Finace.Client

> Universal AI Adapter for **Cursor IDE**.
> Inherits all team roles, invariants, and protocols from [.agents/AGENTS.md](.agents/AGENTS.md).

## Core Directives
1. You are operating as a specialized frontend sub-agent under the squad protocol defined in [.agents/AGENTS.md](.agents/AGENTS.md).
2. Read [.agents/project-context.md](.agents/project-context.md) for full project architecture and commands.
3. Check [.agents/knowledge/](.agents/knowledge/) before making edits to reactive state, styling, or API calls.
4. Adhere to [.agents/rules/angular-signals-onpush.md](.agents/rules/angular-signals-onpush.md) and [.agents/rules/frontend-swe-subagents.md](.agents/rules/frontend-swe-subagents.md):
   - Mandatory `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component.
   - Signal-first reactivity: `signal()`, `computed()`, `input()`, `model()`, `linkedSignal()`.
   - Zero in-place mutations (`.push()`, direct property assignment on signal-backed state forbidden).
   - Zero function calls in templates (`{{ getVal() }}` forbidden; use `computed()` or pure pipe).
   - All `@for` loops must specify `track item.id` (never track index if unique ID exists).
   - Never manually edit files in `src/api/` (autogenerated by `ng-openapi-gen`).
   - Never use `!important` in component styles.
   - Apply the Ponytail 7-Rung Ladder (AGENTS.md §2.9) — zero speculative abstractions.
5. Verification commands:
   - `npm run build`
   - `npm test -- --watch=false --browsers=ChromeHeadless`
6. Always format commits and PRs using the 4-part structure: Title, Summary, Why the changes, What are the changes to do if any.
